Each group k has (2k - 1) numbers, so S(n) = sum from k=1 to n of (2k - 1). Wait a second! I remember that sum of first n odd numbers is n squared. Let me check that: sum from k=1 to n of (2k - 1) = 2*(n(n+1)/2) - n = n(n+1) - n = n². Yes! Perfect, that's a key identity here. So S(n) = n². Wait, let's verify with the groups we have to make sure I didn't mess up.

